WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.280
Christmas! Some know it as the most wonderful&nbsp;
time of the year, a time for snow, hot chocolate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:13.440
family, and a sense of magic in the air. Others&nbsp;
know it as a time of stress, last-minute shopping,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.960
canceled flights, and relatives you’d rather&nbsp;
not be stuck in a room with. No matter how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:25.520
you feel about Christmas, there’s one thing we&nbsp;
can all agree on: it only comes once a year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:31.520
Right? Well, that might be true in most of the&nbsp;
world, but the SCP Foundation came across one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:39.200
particular little town where the Christmas party&nbsp;
never stops, for better or for much, much worse.&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:45.600
SCP-784 is a neighborhood in a small Texas&nbsp;
town, made up of twenty-four houses and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.960
two apartment buildings. Every last one of&nbsp;
them is decorated top to bottom in bright,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:57.360
twinkling Christmas lights. No matter how hot&nbsp;
it is outside, and Texas summers can be brutal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:02.480
the ground is always blanketed with at least&nbsp;
twelve centimeters of snow. Curiously, there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:07.760
is never any visible snowfall happening in the&nbsp;
neighborhood that would explain this. The snow is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:13.600
just always there. It might look inviting from the&nbsp;
outside. A quaint little neighborhood where the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:20.000
snow never melts and the Christmas lights never go&nbsp;
out. But the folks at the SCP Foundation know by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:27.760
now that things are rarely ever what they seem.
All of the houses in SCP-784 are occupied by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:35.120
beings referred to as SCP-784-1. They appear&nbsp;
to be completely ordinary, mostly adult humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:42.240
dressed in traditional Christmas sweaters. There&nbsp;
are approximately 300 people living in SCP-784,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.680
and they appear to age like normal&nbsp;
people, though no deaths of SCP-784-1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:53.360
have ever been observed. The citizens of&nbsp;
SCP-784 spend their time doing activities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:58.720
exclusively associated with Christmas and the&nbsp;
Holiday season. They sing Christmas Carols,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:05.200
perform Christmas pageants, throw eggnog&nbsp;
festivals, give gifts, and decorate their homes.&nbsp;

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.800
When the sun goes down, the activities&nbsp;
turn to acts of Christmas-themed vandalism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:17.440
decorating any object or living thing deemed&nbsp;
“not cheerful enough” by any means necessary.&nbsp;

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:23.440
When a Foundation supply convoy stopped near&nbsp;
SCP-784 for the night in order to refuel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:28.400
they got to experience this maniacal&nbsp;
dedication to the Christmas Spirit first-hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:33.120
First, the Foundation vehicles were egged,&nbsp;
drawing the attention of the personnel on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.640
board. As the Foundation operatives chased off the&nbsp;
egg-based assailants, they left several vehicles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.760
unattended. When they returned, they found their&nbsp;
vehicles and equipment changed into something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:49.040
a bit more festive. First, they noticed that&nbsp;
a Humvee had been converted into a sleigh.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.400
Then, upon checking the inventory of a weapons&nbsp;
shipment on board, they realized the fragmentation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.600
grenades had been replaced with glass Christmas&nbsp;
ornaments, and antlers had been welded onto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:06.400
the 156 safety helmets in their possession.
Unsettled by these changes, and the speed at which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:13.200
the seemingly human instances of SCP-784-1 had&nbsp;
been able to make them, the personnel attempted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:18.640
drive away. When they started their engines, they&nbsp;
were shocked at a loud sputtering sound and bursts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:25.520
of nutmeg-scented smoke. While they were gone,&nbsp;
their fuel tanks had been filled with eggnog.&nbsp;

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:30.800
If this encounter wasn’t enough to demonstrate&nbsp;
that SCP-784 was not to be trifled with,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:34.640
there were several incidents of SCP&nbsp;
Foundation Agents entering the bounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:39.440
of the neighborhood and failing to adequately&nbsp;
perform the required Christmas celebrations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:46.000
When someone’s Christmas Cheer is not up to par,&nbsp;
instances of SCP-784-1 in the vicinity respond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:51.680
immediately and aggressively, incapacitating&nbsp;
the offending person, and forcing them into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:57.520
the nearest house. Five different Foundation&nbsp;
Agents have been abducted in this way so far.&nbsp;

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:03.360
The first Foundation Agent to be abducted was&nbsp;
Agent Paulson. While patrolling through SCP-784,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:08.320
dressed in a Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer&nbsp;
sweater and a Santa hat, Agent Paulson made the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:13.680
grave mistake of wishing a passing person,&nbsp;
“Happy Holidays!” In the blink of an eye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:19.280
the mood around her darkened. Eight stone-faced&nbsp;
people with their Holly Jolly attire surrounded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:25.200
Agent Paulson. She attempted to draw her weapon&nbsp;
to defend herself but simply was not fast enough.&nbsp;

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.440
Thrashing and screaming for help, Agent&nbsp;
Paulson was dragged into a nearby home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:35.520
kicking over an inflatable snowman on the way in.
Next, Agent Matthews was on night patrol when a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:40.960
bout of spontaneous caroling broke out. He joined&nbsp;
in singing Silent Night in an attempt to blend in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:48.480
with the instances of SCP-784-1. Unfortunately,&nbsp;
he misremembered the lyrics to the song and began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:54.480
singing the third verse while everyone else was&nbsp;
on the second. While still singing, the citizens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.480 --> 00:05:00.080
overwhelmed Agent Matthews and tied him up with&nbsp;
a string of decorative red and green lights.&nbsp;

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:05.440
Agent Sanderson, who was supervising the patrol,&nbsp;
attempted to intervene and free Matthews,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:11.200
which attracted the attention of more&nbsp;
instances of SCP-784-1. Both Agents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:16.080
were overwhelmed by the crowd, restrained,&nbsp;
and pulled into a home for what can only be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:21.120
described as Christmas Carol Reprogramming.&nbsp;
Observers heard the sound of Christmas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:27.680
Carols being sung inside for several days after.
While on his patrol, Agent Anderson tripped and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:33.840
stubbed his toe hard against a Santa Claus-themed&nbsp;
lawn gnome. Overwhelmed by pain and irritation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:40.240
Anderson swore loudly and violently for a duration&nbsp;
of fourteen seconds. At the sound of his salty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:47.840
language, three instances of SCP-784-1 sprang into&nbsp;
action and grabbed Anderson before he could react.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:52.240
Two held his body in place, restraining&nbsp;
his arms, and forcing him to his knees.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:56.960
The third held his head still, tilting&nbsp;
it back, and forcing his mouth open.&nbsp;

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:02.080
A fourth instance emerged from a house, carrying&nbsp;
a quart of eggnog. As Anderson struggled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:08.560
to no avail, the eggnog was poured into his mouth&nbsp;
until the quart was empty, and he collapsed limply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:16.480
on the ground. Once he was rendered unconscious,&nbsp;
the instances of SCP-784-1 dragged him inside.&nbsp;

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:20.720
Finally, Agent Davids was observing the&nbsp;
neighborhood when he was offered a present&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:26.640
by one of the few children in the town, a young&nbsp;
girl wearing a sparkly green and red sweater,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:32.800
and a headband decorated with reindeer antlers.&nbsp;
Davids accepted the gift with a forced smile and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:37.200
thanked the little girl, but apparently&nbsp;
did not respond with enough enthusiasm.&nbsp;

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:41.600
When he failed to give the reaction she was&nbsp;
looking for, the little girl tackled him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:46.880
with a surprising amount of force, grabbing him&nbsp;
around his legs and knocking him to the ground.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:51.280
Before he could regain his balance and climb&nbsp;
to his feet, several more children emerged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:56.960
from a nearby house and dragged Davids&nbsp;
inside, pulling him by his arms and legs.&nbsp;

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:01.040
Between one and three days after they were&nbsp;
taken, the abducted personnel emerged from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:06.240
the house they were pulled into. They were all&nbsp;
dressed in new, more elaborate Christmas wear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:11.520
from light-up sweaters to headbands covered in&nbsp;
tiny presents. When a supervisor attempted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:17.040
extract the Foundation personnel, the personnel&nbsp;
refused to leave. When the issue was pressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:24.400
further, the instances of SCP-784-1 around them&nbsp;
became increasingly aggressive, and even violent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:30.960
in their attempt to protect the abducted&nbsp;
agent. Paulson, Matthews, Anderson, Sanderson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:37.920
and Davids are still within the boundaries of&nbsp;
SCP-784 and are considered lost. The official&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:43.200
story is that they died in the line of duty, in&nbsp;
order to protect their families from the truth.&nbsp;

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:49.680
SCP-784-1’s fixation on Christmas Spirit&nbsp;
doesn’t only extend to humans and inanimate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:55.600
objects. Any living being within the walls&nbsp;
of SCP-784 that doesn’t look festive enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:02.400
is subject to a swarm of citizens decorating it,&nbsp;
and that includes animals. During several patrols,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:07.760
Foundation personnel have observed fifteen&nbsp;
stray cats given red collars with a small bell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:12.400
seven stray dogs adorned with reindeer&nbsp;
antlers, rabbits and raccoons with Santa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:18.480
hats forced onto their heads, and even a deer&nbsp;
dressed up to resemble the iconic Rudolph.&nbsp;

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:23.040
Out of an abundance of caution, and in an&nbsp;
attempt to prevent any future abductions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:27.200
there have been extreme limits placed on the&nbsp;
number of staff allowed to patrol inside of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:34.000
SCP-784. The Foundation currently only sends in&nbsp;
agents under special circumstances, most notably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:42.080
for a regular occurrence known as a Noel Event.
About once a month, instances of SCP-784-1 will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:48.160
attempt to exit the boundaries of SCP-784 and&nbsp;
enter a nearby neighborhood in the suburban&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:54.080
community that surrounds 784. Each member of&nbsp;
the community carries a 15-meter-long string&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:59.200
of Christmas lights, and they wander in a group&nbsp;
until they have found an undecorated house.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:03.680
They will begin to promptly decorate this&nbsp;
house, winding the Christmas lights around it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:09.680
until it looks identical to the rest of the&nbsp;
houses in SCP-784. It is unclear what happens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:16.480
to the residents of the chosen house, but it is&nbsp;
likely that they are converted into SCP-784-1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:21.920
much like the abducted Foundation agents.
Naturally, the Foundation has a vested interest in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:28.800
preventing SCP-784 from expanding and is dedicated&nbsp;
to tracking and preventing these Noel Events.&nbsp;

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:34.160
Noel Events do not happen on an exact schedule,&nbsp;
but the Foundation has become aware of certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:41.600
warning signs that one may be coming. Prior to&nbsp;
a Noel Event, SCP-784-1 become more actively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:47.280
festive during the day, notably increasing their&nbsp;
singing, decorating, and eggnog consumption.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:53.680
When these signs have been noted, a select team of&nbsp;
personnel is ordered to execute Procedure 784-C,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:57.440
a preventative measure employed to&nbsp;
stop the Noel Event from occurring.&nbsp;

00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:02.800
When Procedure 784-C has been ordered to&nbsp;
commence, Foundation personnel dress up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:09.920
Santa outfits and position themselves by the exit&nbsp;
points of SCP-784. They sing the classic carol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:15.920
“Good King Wenceslas” and pass out nonalcoholic&nbsp;
eggnog to the other personnel stationed with them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:22.880
Naturally, this draws the attention of SCP-784-1,&nbsp;
unable to resist the allure of holiday cheer and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:28.320
goodwill toward men. Once they have arrived, the&nbsp;
personnel distribute a secondary batch of eggnog&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:35.440
to SCP-784-1, this one mixed with a mild sedative.
After the drugged eggnog has been passed out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:40.960
the Foundation personnel are to sing carols&nbsp;
with the citizens of SCP-784 as the sedative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:47.680
takes effect. As instances of SCP-784-1 begin&nbsp;
to pass out, their neighbors will silently carry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:53.840
them into their designated homes on their&nbsp;
own until all of them have fallen asleep.&nbsp;

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:59.360
If Procedure 784-C happens to fail for&nbsp;
any reason, the Foundation personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:04.160
are instructed to release a sleeping gas into&nbsp;
the town and restrain the citizens until they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:09.680
have been rendered unconscious. Then, they are&nbsp;
all to be placed in their homes by personnel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:15.040
If the members of any nearby communities express&nbsp;
concern, a standard cover story of a neighborhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.680
football watch party gone a little too far - AKA&nbsp;
“Drunken Football” is released to the public.&nbsp;

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:25.360
In order to prevent civilians from accidentally&nbsp;
happening upon SCP-784, the neighborhood has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:32.160
disguised as an ordinary gated community. It is&nbsp;
surrounded by a 3.5-meter-high, 0.8-meter-thick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:37.600
concrete wall, topped with an electrified steel&nbsp;
cable. The Foundation is not allowed to prevent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:42.480
non-Foundation personnel from entering, in order&nbsp;
to mitigate the risk of a violent reaction from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:48.400
SCP-784-1. However, when an individual&nbsp;
not related to the Foundation is spotted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:54.400
leaving the neighborhood, they are to be swiftly&nbsp;
detained, interrogated, and given an amnestic.&nbsp;

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:58.960
No Foundation personnel are permitted to enter the&nbsp;
neighborhood unless they are dressed in Christmas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:04.320
attire. These personnel must also be armed with&nbsp;
the knowledge of all basic Christmas Carols.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:08.720
The area is to be monitored at all times via&nbsp;
a Foundation-owned weather balloon, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:15.840
citizens of SCP-784 are to be watched for unusual&nbsp;
behavior and the signs of an impending Noel Event.&nbsp;

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:22.800
SCP-784 is currently classified as Euclid, and is&nbsp;
considered to be largely non-threatening as long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:29.120
as it continues to be contained. The citizens&nbsp;
of SCP-784 are not overtly harming anyone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:33.760
and they don’t seem to want anything more&nbsp;
than to celebrate Christmas forever. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:38.240
it’s uncertain how far they would attempt to&nbsp;
expand if Noel Events were allowed to occur&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:42.480
with no intervention. Perhaps&nbsp;
they would expand forever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:47.840
forcing eggnog down throats and strangling&nbsp;
houses with twinkling lights, turning the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:53.600
as we know it into a twisted snow globe.&nbsp;
Hopefully, we’ll never have to find out.&nbsp;

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:57.600
Just be careful if you’re wandering through&nbsp;
the suburbs of Texas and hear the jingling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:04.000
of sleigh bells in July, or you might&nbsp;
find yourself on SCP-784’s Naughty List.&nbsp;

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:09.520
Now go check out “Trapped in a Game -&nbsp;
SCP-1733 - Season Opener” and “The Skin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:18.080
Stealers - SCP-3333 - Tower” for more&nbsp;
places you hope to never find yourself!

